| ============================================================================
| apfelbauer Detection Rules for Splunk
| Targeting Apple Intelligence enablement primitives and related framework-access patterns
| ============================================================================
| Data model: Splunk CIM Endpoint fields (process_name, process_path,
| command_line, parent_process_name, parent_process_path, dest, _time)
| Adjust field names for your data source (FDR, osquery, Jamf Protect, etc.)
| ============================================================================


| ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
| Rule 1: Silent Apple Intelligence Enablement via defaults write
| Name: apfelbauer - Silent AI Enablement (CloudSubscriptionFeatures)
| Description: Detects writes to com.apple.CloudSubscriptionFeatures.optIn
|   via the defaults command. This preference silently enables Apple
|   Intelligence and is not written by legitimate software.
| Severity: Critical
| MITRE ATT&CK: T1562.001 - Disable or Modify Tools
| ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

index=endpoint sourcetype=*endpoint* process_name="defaults"
  (command_line="*write*" AND command_line="*com.apple.CloudSubscriptionFeatures.optIn*")
| table _time dest user parent_process_name process_name command_line
| sort - _time


| ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
| Rule 2: DSID Harvesting via MobileMeAccounts Read
| Name: apfelbauer - DSID Harvesting (MobileMeAccounts)
| Description: Detects non-Settings processes reading MobileMeAccounts
|   preferences to extract the DSID for the Apple Intelligence enablement
|   bypass on macOS 26.4+.
| Severity: High
| MITRE ATT&CK: T1552.001 - Credentials in Files
| ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

index=endpoint sourcetype=*endpoint* process_name="defaults"
  (command_line="*read*" AND command_line="*MobileMeAccounts*")
  NOT parent_process_name IN ("System Settings","systempreferences","ManagedClient","mdmclient")
| table _time dest user parent_process_name process_name command_line
| sort - _time


| ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
| Rule 3: Darwin Notification Trigger for AI Enablement
| Name: apfelbauer - Darwin Notification Trigger (OptIn.Changed)
| Description: Detects use of notifyutil to post the
|   CloudSubscriptionFeatures.OptIn.Changed Darwin notification, which forces
|   the daemon to re-evaluate the attacker-written enablement preference.
|  
| Severity: Critical
| MITRE ATT&CK: T1562.001 - Disable or Modify Tools
| ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

index=endpoint sourcetype=*endpoint* process_name="notifyutil"
  (command_line="*-p*" AND command_line="*com.apple.CloudSubscriptionFeatures.OptIn.Changed*")
| table _time dest user parent_process_name process_name command_line
| sort - _time


| ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
| Rule 4: FoundationModels Framework Load from Unsigned Process
| Name: apfelbauer - FoundationModels Unsigned Load
| Description: Detects loading of FoundationModels.framework by unsigned
|   or non-Apple-signed processes. Requires library/image load telemetry.
|  
| Severity: High
| MITRE ATT&CK: T1059.004 - Unix Shell
| ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

index=endpoint sourcetype=*endpoint* EventType="ImageLoad"
  ImageLoaded="*FoundationModels.framework*"
  NOT process_path IN ("/System/Library/*","/usr/libexec/*")
  NOT process_name IN ("Siri","siriinferenced","siriactionsd","Shortcuts","Xcode")
| table _time dest user process_name process_path ImageLoaded
| sort - _time


| ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
| Rule 5: Swift Interpreter from Non-Xcode Parent
| Name: apfelbauer - Swift from Non-Xcode Parent
| Description: Detects /usr/bin/swift invoked by a scripting interpreter or
|   shell rather than the Xcode toolchain, indicating potential use as a
|   bridge to FoundationModels.framework.
| Severity: Medium
| MITRE ATT&CK: T1059.004 - Unix Shell
| ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

index=endpoint sourcetype=*endpoint* process_name="swift" process_path="/usr/bin/swift"
  parent_process_name IN ("python3","python","bash","zsh","sh","ruby","perl","node","osascript")
  NOT parent_process_path IN ("*/Xcode.app/*","*/xcodebuild","*/xcrun")
| table _time dest user parent_process_name parent_process_path process_name command_line
| sort - _time


| ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
| Rule 6: Writes to com.apple.generativeexperiencesd (surface probing indicator)
| Name: apfelbauer - Writes to generativeexperiencesd Prefs (Probe Indicator)
| Description: Detects writes to com.apple.generativeexperiencesd preferences.
|   This preference domain is user-writable, but static analysis of the dylib
|   that generativeexperiencesd runs (GenerativeExperiencesRuntime on macOS
|   26.5 Beta) does NOT confirm that any key in this domain (e.g.
|   disableToolBoxAllowList, inputValidation, safetyMode,
|   bypassTranscriptWriteRedaction) is read by the daemon. Absent a confirmed
|   reader, writes here are best treated as a LOW-CONFIDENCE signal of an
|   attacker probing AI preferences, not proof of safety-control bypass.
|  
| Severity: Low
| MITRE ATT&CK: T1647 - Plist File Modification
| ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

index=endpoint sourcetype=*endpoint* process_name="defaults"
  (command_line="*write*" AND command_line="*com.apple.generativeexperiencesd*")
| table _time dest user parent_process_name process_name command_line
| sort - _time


| ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
| Rule 7: Rapid Sequential Shell Execution from Swift Interpreter
| Name: apfelbauer - Rapid Shell Exec from Swift
| Description: Detects multiple child processes spawned by the Swift
|   interpreter within a 10-second window, consistent with LLM tool callbacks
|   executing commands in rapid succession.
| Severity: Medium
| MITRE ATT&CK: T1059.004 - Unix Shell
| ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

index=endpoint sourcetype=*endpoint*
  parent_process_name="swift" parent_process_path="/usr/bin/swift"
  process_name IN ("sh","bash","zsh","cat","ls","find","curl","whoami","hostname","env","grep","awk","sed","defaults","security","dscl")
| bin _time span=10s
| stats count as exec_count dc(process_name) as unique_cmds values(process_name) as commands values(command_line) as cmdlines by _time dest parent_process_path
| where exec_count >= 3 AND unique_cmds >= 2
| sort - _time
